    {
      "id": "s9",
      "kind": "content",
      "heading": "Beyond CB1 and CB2",
      "narration": "The picture continues to grow. Anandamide also activates TRPV1, the ion channel that responds to heat and to capsaicin from chilli peppers. Other proteins, such as the orphan receptor GPR55 and the nuclear receptors called PPARs, respond to some cannabinoids as well. In 1998, Ben-Shabat and Mechoulam showed that related lipids released together with 2-AG, which do not bind the receptor themselves, can increase the activity of 2-AG, and coined the term entourage effect. The endocannabinoid system, first revealed by the chemistry of a plant, is now understood as a widespread lipid signalling system of the vertebrate body, and research on it continues.",
